'Offline prompt augmentation — keyboard typos in user-typed spans.\n\n\nThe only consumer is ``grpo_train.py`` (``--typo-share``): a fraction of the\nTRAIN pool gets its prompts lightly corrupted with keyboard-adjacent typos\n(augmentex ``CharAug(action="typo")``), simulating a user who misses a\nneighbouring key. The reward stays intact — it compares the model\'s answer\nagainst the clean reference — and the whole GRPO group sees the same\ncorrupted prompt, so within-group advantages stay unbiased.\n\n``CharAug(action="typo")``)\n\nInvariants\n\n* **Train-only**: ``augment_pool`` is applied to the train split ONLY — the\n  val/test hold-outs are the measuring instrument and stay clean.\n* **Payload intact**: typos land only in spans a user could plausibly\n  keyboard-type (per-class boundary table in :func:`typed_spans`); external\n  context (retrieved documents, the text to summarise, tool results, the\n  SGR date preamble, tool schemas in ``system``) is never touched.\n* **Light by construction**: at most ``max_aug`` (default 2) character\n  substitutions per typed span, hard-checked via Levenshtein distance —\n  an attempt that exceeds the budget is reverted, never kept.\n* **Exact share**: ``share`` is the exact fraction of eligible prompts that\n  end up carrying ≥1 visible typo (retry-until-changed, ≤ ``max_attempts``\n  deterministic reseeds; a span that refuses to change after all attempts\n  leaves the example clean).\n* **Two modes** (`TypoConfig.copies`): ``copies == 0`` — in-place replacement\n  (``share`` of the pool corrupted, size unchanged); ``copies > 0`` —\n  multi-variant (the clean original + ``copies`` augmented copies,\n  ``(copies + 1)·N`` in total, each copy corrupting ``share`` independently).\n* **Deterministic**: every random choice derives from\n  ``f"{seed}:{task_class}:{source}#{occurrence}"`` (mirroring the per-class\n  seeding convention of :mod:`llm_training.build`); augmentex\'s global RNG\n  (``random`` + ``numpy.random``) is saved, reseeded and restored around\n  every call, so the augmentation is replayable regardless of what else\n  consumes those globals.\n* **System-prompt dimension** (``TypoConfig.system_share`` /\n  :func:`llm_training.augment.typo.augment_pool_system`): an orthogonal\n  instruction-noise-robustness augmentation — light typos in the SYSTEM\n  prompt (the task instruction) of the :data:`SYSTEM_TYPO_CLASSES` allowlist,\n  with the ``<tools>`` block and fenced code/JSON never touched.'
